# MANIFEST.sha256 - frozen/
#
# One line per code and data file of this directory, with two hashes:
#
#   <sha256 of the tagged file>  <sha256 of the shipped file>  <path>
#
# and, between brackets, what separates the two files and the git tag
# (for one file, a commit) and path of the tagged one. The first hash is
# the one the data files of the package record.
#   submitted-v1              the code that produced the submitted figure
#   submitted-v1-postproc     the original post-processing
#   runner-v13                the last tagged version of the job runner
#   analysis-plan-enmienda-1  modified encoders: models, selection runs
#   the tags on the lines of harness_seed_a.py, _b.py and _c.py
#                             modified encoders: harness of seeds A, B and C
#                             (the first also froze the entry rule)
#   e1-t10-v1                 modified encoders: the comparisons
#   05d7c00                   a commit, not a tag: the script of the two
#                             tables of the modified encoders
#
# COMMENTS REMOVED            Python file without its comments; the
#                             abstract syntax tree equals that of the
#                             tagged file
# COMMENTS AND NOTES REMOVED  the same, and docstrings that held
#                             working notes were shortened; the
#                             abstract syntax tree, docstrings aside,
#                             equals that of the tagged file
# MESSAGE TEXTS EDITED        the same, and the wording of some
#                             messages and notes was edited; the
#                             abstract syntax tree equals that of the
#                             tagged file once those docstrings and
#                             the text of those strings are set aside
# NOTES REMOVED               data file without its free-text working
#                             notes; every value that defines a job
#                             or a stream is unchanged
# IDENTICAL                   byte-identical to the tagged file
# DIFFERS                     NOT derived from the tagged file as
#                             described above
#
# This file is annotated and is not in sha256sum format; the plain list
# that `sha256sum -c` reads is SHA256SUMS, next to it.
#
